solution.text:
Given,
$$
\begin{array}{l}
x_{1}=A \sin \left(\omega t+\frac{\pi}{6}\right) \\
x_{2}=A \cos (\omega t) \\
x_{2}=A \operatorname{sin}\left(\omega t+\frac{\pi}{2}\right)
\end{array}
$$
Phase difference
$$
\Delta \phi=\phi_{2}-\phi_{1}
$$
$$
\begin{array}{l}
\Delta \phi=\frac{\pi}{2}-\frac{\pi}{6} \\
\Delta \phi=\frac{3 \pi-\pi}{6}=\frac{\pi}{3}
\end{array}
$$
